# TX2-F1 (W-TX2 on snap15; writer 10): W-TX2's minimal text, scratch/tx2/min/holiday2027.tally. L §5.14 on d: "A movement whose day is a hole makes every flows and binding over a span it might fall in a hole
# (G-MP-2). A day that is a hole and not a window has no bound, so that is every span, earlier ones included, whatever
# the instance's `when` says: its booking cut min(t, K) is a hole with it"; E §4.2 Holes in the walk: "from the first
# day it may fall on (every day, for a day that is a hole and not a window)".
# q_hand_when_2025 and q_konto2_2025 are now the hole (snap15: 0.00 and 0.00); the other lines are as snap15 printed
# them (scratch/tx2/min/holiday2027.out).
=== m.tally
model holiday2027
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-15
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
  note "W-TX2's minimal text for E1-02's 2027 holiday: a monthly payment on the 5th, rolled to the next business day, under a calendar whose 2027 Spring Day is one of two April Mondays. by_schedule rolls with schedule (B's ola_order, flat.tally:177-180); by_hand rolls with is_business and add_business (B's mtg_pay, flat.tally:221). Each ask reads 2025's flows only."

source card "W-TX2's made-up card"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

place payer: outside lives 2025-01-01..

place konto: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place konto2: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place konto3: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place konto4: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

input amt: money DUK

input cal: calendar

input dom: int

input live: bool

move by_schedule[m in months]: transfers
  on schedule(m, dom, following, cal)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from payer to konto amount amt

move by_hand[m in months]: transfers
  on if is_business(day_of(m, dom), cal) then day_of(m, dom) else add_business(day_of(m, dom), 1, cal)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from payer to konto amount amt

move by_hand_when[m in months]: transfers
  on if is_business(day_of(m, dom), cal) then day_of(m, dom) else add_business(day_of(m, dom), 1, cal)
  at start_of(m)
  when live
  leg cash from payer to konto2 amount amt

move by_hand_dec[m in months]: transfers
  on if is_business(day_of(m, dom), cal) then day_of(m, dom) else add_business(day_of(m, dom), 1, cal)
  at start_of(m)
  reads konto
  leg cash from payer to konto amount min(amt, max(amt, bal(konto)))

ask q_hand_when_2025: flows(by_hand_when, 2025) law 2025-12-31

ask q_hand_dec_2025: flows(by_hand_dec, 2025) law 2025-12-31

ask q_konto_2025: bal(konto, 2025-12-31) law 2025-12-31

ask q_konto2_2025: bal(konto2, 2025-12-31) law 2025-12-31

def due[m in months]: date = day_of(m, dom) at start_of(m)

def on_live[m in months]: bool = not live at start_of(m)

move by_hand_at[m in months]: transfers
  on if is_business(day_of(m, dom), cal) then day_of(m, dom) else add_business(day_of(m, dom), 1, cal)
  at due[m]
  leg cash from payer to konto3 amount amt

move by_hand_def_when[m in months]: transfers
  on if is_business(day_of(m, dom), cal) then day_of(m, dom) else add_business(day_of(m, dom), 1, cal)
  at start_of(m)
  when on_live[m]
  leg cash from payer to konto4 amount amt

ask q_hand_at_2025: flows(by_hand_at, 2025), bal(konto3, 2025-12-31) law 2025-12-31

ask q_hand_def_when_2025: flows(by_hand_def_when, 2025), bal(konto4, 2025-12-31) law 2025-12-31

ask q_schedule_2025: flows(by_schedule, 2025) law 2025-12-31

ask q_hand_2025: flows(by_hand, 2025) law 2025-12-31

ask q_schedule_day: by_schedule[2027-04].day law 2025-12-31

version card_rows
  cite card
  governs 2025..2027
  known 2025-01-01
  amt = 100.00 "card"
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun]) governs 2025..2026 "card"
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [one_of([2027-04-05, 2027-04-12])]) governs 2027 "card: Spring Day 2027 not yet set"
  dom = 5 "card"
  live = false "card: the payment never runs"
=== expect
